    "Only normal screen render state and fixed 72/144 dpi were tested; rollover/down, printing, other zoom grids, optional-content state and all PDF annotation variants remain unverified.",
    "Widget/XFA form appearance rendering is not included and explicitly blocks acceptance.",
    "Strict zero-delta comparison rejects even the observed one-level normal-alpha compositor rounding mismatch. No relaxed tolerance or per-input compositor calibration.",
    "Original opaque control contains one visible stamp plus one invisible link. Native ordering with multiple simultaneously visible overlapping annotations is not validated by this control.",
    "Per-annotation full-canvas alpha and page-native render keep original coordinates and native clipping. No broad clipping-support claim is made; clipping-specific annotation fixture is not included.",
    "Zero visible ink does not certify annotation link semantics or browser interaction retention.",
    "Native source/crop images are private diagnostics only. No public uploads, holdout selection, browser audit, Codex CLI/API or independent Codex task occurred.",
    "A /Dest key exists on all three diagnostic links but PDFium cannot resolve the destination in these loaded inputs. Do not infer that the full original documents lack destinations.",
    "Public summaries contain only metadata counts and extraction status. Native coordinates, destination parameters and actual target strings remain in private results. No link target was fetched, opened or executed.",
    "FPDFLink_GetDest can resolve GoTo actions too; link_destination counts and action_destination counts are not disjoint categories."
